  "reason": "Evidence: The RNA encoder choice has shown the largest single-factor improvement so far (pca_n2000 → scvi_n200 yielded +3.9% acc in the multimodal setting: 0.639 → 0.678). The current best config (config_031: scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted, resnet50) achieves 0.678 acc. Uncertainty: It is unknown whether scgpt, a more expressive pre-trained RNA encoder, can further improve on scvi_n200 in this multimodal context. Question tested: Does replacing scvi_n200 with scgpt (all other hyperparameters held at their known-best values: multiprofile, avgpool, weighted, resnet50) yield a further accuracy gain? Why this is the best next experiment: It is a clean single-variable extension of the most productive design axis identified so far (RNA encoder quality), keeps all other knobs at their validated optima, and directly determines whether the RNA encoder dimension still has headroom to exploit before investing budget in less-certain axes like the image encoder (which showed very weak standalone signal at 0.208 acc)."
}

